`timescale 1ns/1ps

// QNSC wrapper of m_qnsc_p_bus: the QSoC P_BUS (APB4 peripheral bus).
// Spec: QNSC_PBUS_MAS on the team SharePoint.
//
// Edit this .src.sv, then `make wrap BLOCK=pbus`: emacs verilog-mode expands
// the AUTO comments and writes rtl/m_qnsc_wrap_pbus.sv, the file pbus.f compiles.
// Template functions: doc/rules/EMACS_quick_guide.pdf.
//
// The core is m_qnsc_p_bus, generated by APB-BUS-Generator from
// util/gen/p_bus/p_bus.xlsx (recipe util/gen/p_bus/gen.sh). One master, the
// AXI2APB bridge, 18-bit address (contract meta.pbus_paddr_width); fourteen
// slaves APB_M0..M13, 14-bit offset each (meta.apb_paddr_width). There is no
// bridge: both sides already speak APB.
//
// What this wrapper does, and nothing else:
//   - names the ports by Naming Rule 3.3: the input side is the APB port the
//     bridge drives, i_bus_apb_s_0_* / o_bus_apb_s_0_*; slave n is
//     o_bus_apb_m_<n>_* / i_bus_apb_m_<n>_*, n = the contract port APB_Mn;
//   - ties i_clk/i_rstn: with one master every arbiter is plain assignments
//     and the decoder is combinational, so the router has no flip-flop and
//     P_BUS has no clock or reset port (QNSC_PBUS_MAS);
//   - ties the generator's sideband inputs (pprot, protect_en, slverr_en) and
//     leaves their outputs open: AXI2APB drives no PPROT, and each slave's
//     PPROT is tied in design/top (QNSC_PBUS_MAS, "No PPROT through P_BUS").
//
// A wrapper is IP (design/README.md, "Shared numbers: who may use qnsc_pkg"):
// no import, no parameter. The address map lives in the generated core, not here.

module m_qnsc_wrap_pbus
(
